<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46514" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sulfur</span></b>  (in MSS. also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sulphur</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sulpur</span></b> ),
			ŭris, n. (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>masc.</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Prax. 16</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 1, 38 <i>med.</i></span></i>), <i>brimstone</i>, <i>sulphur.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 35,
				15, 50, § 174</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cato, R.
				R. 39, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 8, 5, 11</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vivum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 39, 13, 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 4, 739</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lucr. 6,
			221</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 748</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">6, 807</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tib. 1, 5,
				11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Prop. 4</span></i> (5), 8, 86; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 5,
				405</span></i> et saep.—<i>Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 449</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vivacia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					3, 374</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lurida,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 791</span></i>
			; 15, 351; <i><span class="en">Quint. 12, 10, 76</span></i> Spald. <i>N. cr.;</i> used as a cement, <i><span class="en">Juv. 5,
			48</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <b>poet.</b>, <i>lightning</i> (so called from its sulphureous
			smell): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aethereum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					7, 160</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">satrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					2, 24</span></i>
			.</div>
